<h2>Who you are working with</h2>
<p>I’m Jaylan, and I operate <Wordmark inline/> personally in Tennessee. My services cover websites and advertising, document creation, and IT support for homes and businesses.</p>
<h2>What your project needs to define</h2>
<p>Your written project agreement will cover the scope of work, deliverables, review process, timeline, payment milestones, ownership, third-party services, and support arrangements. Cancellation and refund arrangements also need to be set out before you agree to paid work.</p>
<h2>Current website behavior</h2>
<p>Inquiry forms prepare requests for you to review, copy, open in Gmail or your device’s email app, or download. They do not send automatically or create tracked tickets. The portfolio contains fictional business concepts. Sample shopping bags, table requests, and project previews do not place orders or reservations. The site does not currently create client accounts, accept payments, receive private file uploads, or confirm bookings.</p>
<p>The <a href="/legal/privacy/">privacy information</a> explains how the forms and browser preferences work. The <a href="/legal/refunds/">refund and cancellation page</a> describes the arrangements that still need to be agreed for a project.</p>
<h2>Document services</h2>
<p>Document work includes organizing your information and formatting your material. For agreements, that means preparing your facts and questions for an attorney or formatting language your attorney has supplied or approved. I do not offer legal advice or guarantee that a document is legally sufficient or enforceable.</p>
<h2>Questions about the terms</h2>
<p>Ask me about anything you would like clarified before agreeing to a project. This page does not establish deposit, refund, ownership, warranty, or liability terms.</p>
